From e0f1da9bc320be151a210bdbe6008774f9145d4c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ziling Zhou <106626435+Ziling-Zhou@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 16:47:17 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] frontend: Home: Let plugins handle Delete for their
 clusters

Delete in the Home page's cluster action menu only removes a cluster
from the kubeconfig. For a cluster a plugin created, such as a local
minikube cluster, that leaves the cluster running, so the plugin has
to add its own Delete item to the menu.

Add registerClusterProviderDeleteHandler, exported from the plugin
SDK with its ClusterDeleteHandler type. A handler names the clusters
it owns and one of its registered dialogs; for those clusters Delete
opens that dialog instead of the kubeconfig confirmation. The first
handler that owns a cluster wins, a handler that throws owns nothing,
and Delete for other clusters behaves as before. A handler is ignored
unless owns is a function and its dialog is neither empty nor
deleteDynamic, the built-in confirmation, which the menu would
otherwise open as well.

